; ted-tokit-reads-past-line (#386): the tokeniser compares keyword names
; beyond the end of the line, into the next row of the character map.
; Line 1 "ab", 122 blanks, "Pri" (127 characters), line 2 "nt".  A blank
; typed at column 2 moves "Pri" to the columns 126-128; leaving the line
; tokenises it from the character map; SAVE.  Correct: "Pri" stays text;
; the original reads "nt" of the next row and saves the token Print.
; Fixed in TED-C: the name comparison stops at the end of the line.
; @fixed #386
; @file bo.bas "ab                                                                                                                          Pri\nnt\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @expect data bo.bas "a b                                                                                                                          Pri\x00nt\x00"
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
key 4e
type " "
key 4d
dump after
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
